winex11.drv, winewayland.drv: Do not map layered windows below constant alpha 8.

A layered window whose LWA_ALPHA constant alpha is below 8 (about 3%)
shows nothing a user can see, yet it still takes compositor space and
pointer input, and a compositor that blurs behind translucent windows
draws a blurred band through it. Applications use such near-transparent
windows as resize grips or glow strips around their main window.

Do not map the X11 window while LWA_ALPHA is below 8. On Wayland, treat
a layered window whose saved alpha multiplier is below 8/255 as invisible
when selecting its surface role.

Leave the Windows visibility style intact, so raising the alpha later
maps the window again through the normal window state update.

Applies to: Valve Wine fda79a5 (GE-Proton11-12) after GE's preparation, in order after 0009.

--- a/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c
+++ b/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c
@@ -3838,6 +3838,21 @@
         new_style &= ~WS_VISIBLE;
     }
 
+    /* a layered window below about 3% constant alpha is not shown: invisible, and a blurring
+     * compositor would draw its background through it */
+    if ((new_style & WS_VISIBLE) && (ex_style & WS_EX_LAYERED) && data->layered)
+    {
+        COLORREF key;
+        DWORD flags;
+        BYTE alpha;
+
+        if (NtUserGetLayeredWindowAttributes( hwnd, &key, &alpha, &flags ) && (flags & LWA_ALPHA) && alpha < 8)
+        {
+            TRACE( "win %p/%lx has constant alpha %u, not mapping\n", hwnd, data->whole_window, alpha );
+            new_style &= ~WS_VISIBLE;
+        }
+    }
+
     XFlush( gdi_display );  /* make sure painting is done before we move the window */
 
     if (use_force_below_hack())
--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/window.c
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/window.c
@@ -410,6 +410,10 @@
         (client || wayland_surface_has_hwnd_dmabuf_content(surface)))
         visible = TRUE;
 
+    /* a layered window below about 3% constant alpha is not shown: invisible, and a blurring
+     * compositor would draw its background through it */
+    if ((exstyle & WS_EX_LAYERED) && data->alpha_multiplier < (UINT32_MAX / 0xff) * 8) visible = FALSE;
+
     if (visible && !owner_surface && !use_layer_shell && !toplevel_surface &&
         !rect_intersects_virtual_screen(&data->rects.window) &&
         !should_keep_minimized_toplevel_mapped(surface, style))
